# Procedure for Metaplex DAO Process Proposals 

TLDR: The Metaplex Foundation will implement the following procedure for Metaplex DAO process proposals (“DAO Process Proposals”).

DAO Process Proposals cover changes to the proposal procedures, guidelines and voting parameters for the Metaplex DAO in accordance with the Metaplex DAO Constitution ([https\://www\.metaplex.foundation/metaplex-dao-constitution](https://www.metaplex.foundation/metaplex-dao-constitution)). Please review the DAO Constitution before submitting a DAO Process Proposal. 

The following are the current proposal procedures for:

* Metaplex Improvement Proposals (“MIPs”) for extending or modifying the Metaplex Protocol (https\://github.com/metaplex-foundation/mip/blob/main/mip-5.md).  
* Metaplex Treasury Proposals (“MTPs”) for administration of the DAO’s on-chain treasury (https\://github.com/metaplex-foundation/dao/blob/main/treasury-proposals.md).   
* Proposals for Community Grants from the Metaplex DAO (“Grants”) https\://github.com/metaplex-foundation/dao/blob/main/mplx-grants.md. 

**Proposals.** Anyone may propose a DAO Process Proposal by: (1) completing a DAO Process Proposal form; and (2) proving ownership of 5,000 \$MPLX (subject to revision by Metaplex Foundation based on the market price of \$MPLX). Proposals should provide sufficient details for the community to consider, including a well thought out explanation for the proposed change. 

**Community Feedback & Initial Review.** The community will be able to provide feedback on proposed DAO Process Proposals on the Metaplex Foundation Github Repo. The Metaplex Foundation will screen out proposals that are spam, made in bad faith, would violate the DAO Constitution, or would violate any applicable laws or regulations. If valid counter-proposals are submitted during the community feedback period, the original proposal and all valid counter-proposals will be voted on via a single multiple choice vote.

**Voting Period.** Following the community feedback period, the DAO Council will open the voting period. Voting will be based on \$MPLX ownership, meaning that one \$MPLX equals one vote. The Metaplex Foundation will specify the minimum number of total votes that must be submitted for the vote to count. Approval requires that total (a) "Yes" votes cast exceeds the specified minimum number of votes; and (b) the approval threshold is met (\>50% "Yes" for single proposal votes and a plurality of "Yes" votes for multiple choice votes).

**Implementation.** If approved by the community via a DAO vote, then the DAO Council will update the applicable DAO process and documentation according to the approved proposal’s specifications. 

The Metaplex Foundation may change the procedure for submitting and reviewing DAO Process Proposals based on experience and community feedback as long as the changes do not conflict with previously approved Metaplex Process Proposals ("MPP") or the DAO Constitution (https\://www\.metaplex.foundation/metaplex-dao-constitution).  
**\# Full Procedure for Proposals for Metaplex DAO Process Proposals** 

This procedure applies to community proposals for changes to the DAO’s proposal procedures, guidelines and voting parameters in accordance with the Metaplex DAO Constitution ([https\://www\.metaplex.foundation/metaplex-dao-constitution](https://www.metaplex.foundation/metaplex-dao-constitution)). 

Examples of DAO Process Proposals might include:

* community feedback period duration  
* voting period duration  
* \$MPLX needed to submit proposals  
* process for counter-proposals and multi-choice voting

## **Proposals**

Any \$MPLX holder (the “Original Proposer”) may propose a DAO Process Proposal to the Metaplex repository (currently Github, located here: (https\://github.com/metaplex-foundation/mip/) (the “Repo”) by visiting the Metaplex governance website (https\://mip.metaplex.foundation) and (1) completing a DAO Procedure Proposal form; and (2) proving ownership of 5,000 \$MPLX (subject to revision by Metaplex Foundation based on the market price of MPLX).

By submitting a proposal form, you consent to the information you include being shared with the community for purposes of considering the proposal. You further acknowledge agreement to our privacy policy (https\://dao.metaplex.com/privacy).

The DAO Procedure Proposal form will require the following information to be completed fully and accurately:

### Title  
A concise title describing the proposal. This title will appear as the header of your proposal’s detail page and the community feedback thread generated for your proposal.

### Abstract  
Short explanation of the proposal. 

### Motivation   
How will it benefit the DAO and Metaplex ecosystem? What problems does it solve? What is the expected outcome?

### Detailed Description

Elaborate on the details for the proposal. Introduce and explain concepts. Provide representative examples that show how this proposal will work.

## **Submitting a Proposal**  
After filling out every field in the proposal form to the best of your abilities and connecting your wallet to demonstrate ownership of 5,000 \$MPLX, click Submit proposal.

## **Community Feedback & Initial Review**  
Each DAO Process Proposal will trigger a 7 day “Community Feedback Period”, during which anyone may comment on the proposal in the Repo or submit a counter-proposal. This will provide time for the community to voice its opinion on each proposal before a DAO vote is held.

During the Community Feedback Period, the Metaplex Foundation will review the proposals to screen out ones that are spam, made in bad faith, would violate the DAO Constitution, or would violate any applicable laws or regulations.

The Metaplex Foundation’s goal is to complete an initial screening decision for each proposal within 3 days of publication on the Repo. If we are unable to meet that goal for any particular proposal, we will publish an update on the Repo with a new target date for our decision. If the Metaplex Foundation screens out a proposal it will post the rationale for doing so on the Repo. Proposals that are screened out will be removed from consideration.

The Original Proposer may propose changes to the proposal or withdraw the proposal at any time prior to the end of the Community Feedback Period.

## **Voting Period**  
At the end of the 7-day Community Feedback Period, the Metaplex Foundation will finalize language for the proposed DAO Process Proposal based on the community feedback. The proposed DAO Process Proposal will receive a Metaplex Process Proposal number (e.g., MPP-001).

Voting on materially similar proposals will be grouped so that an original proposal and any valid counter-proposals are voted on by the DAO at the same time. The Metaplex Foundation will use its discretion to group votes to avoid confusion and potentially conflicting results.

The “Voting Period” for a proposal will be open for 5 days. If any valid counter-proposals were submitted, the voting will be via a single multiple choice vote for all valid proposals, including a "No Action" option.

When the DAO Council opens the Voting Period, it will specify the minimum number of total votes that must be submitted for the vote to count (the “Voting Threshold”). Voting will be based on MPLX ownership, meaning that one MPLX equals one vote. The Metaplex Foundation will announce via Twitter (@MetaplexFndn) and on the Metaplex Discord channel when a Voting Period is beginning and direct the community to where it can cast votes on the Metaplex DAO. The voting mechanics may change in the future as we learn from experience.

If only one proposal is voted on by the DAO, to pass it will require both: (a) \> 50% "Yes" votes; and (b) sufficient "Yes" votes to reach quorum. If the vote is multiple choice, assuming quorum is met, the option that receives the most votes will pass.

## **Implementation**

After the DAO Process Proposal has been approved by the DAO, the DAO Council will update the applicable DAO process and documentation according to the approved proposal’s specifications. 

\*\*Disclaimer.\*\* The Metaplex Foundation may terminate a proposal for a DAO Process Proposal at any point in the process if it comes into conflict with applicable laws or regulations.
